+Notification modes are `off`, `on` (`💾 Memory updated`), and `verbose`.
+Mutations are accumulated by logical turn, so one user turn produces at most one
+visible memory notification even if foreground handling performs several writes
+or the bounded reviewer revisits the same turn. Same-value/no-op updates stay
+quiet. Verbose notifications contain at most a compact defense-in-depth
+redacted preview; shared-chat notifications are generic and never reveal
+private memory content. Notification messages are marked internal and are not
+used as recall or reviewer evidence.
 
